Hi Patrick,

I kept the three job-title sketches in the attached deck (CWR-DR-20250410-BRF=
-01 v1.0) and put the card moves on the slide after the Desk Dispatcher compa=
rison. That was where we switched to reading by handoff frequency. The two De=
sk Dispatchers had handoffs in one and five of their last five shifts, and th=
ey needed different evidence for the checks they made.

I kept UX-042 on the higher-frequency side with the route and planned window =
at the start. In the participant's account, the check against Vehicle came la=
ter, after the coordinator's spoken answer. That card still needs its own ent=
ry alongside UX-037, even though both had handoffs in most of their shifts.

For this internal read, if we don't have the handoff count for someone's last=
 five shifts, leave them unassigned. Three shifts is a working boundary for c=
omparing the accounts. We left recruitment and external use of the boundary o=
pen.

Thanks,
Jennifer

